16c14e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-39791" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2}-8}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3}{2(x+2)(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)(x-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the two solutions $x=-2$ and $x=2.$ Therefore, the equations of the vertical asymptotes are $x=-2$ and $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39791/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60c99086-75e7-5d91-b425-4e1b6f582bcc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39791"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39793/selection/390fd85541da345662d60af73357478ba9af6adedb24874b4dcb74a371c5519f" :answer/id #uuid "c671d6ff-b201-592f-984f-c8b6350a7cc2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,x=1,\\,x=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39793/selection/dab6bca13f296cb6500ebc2a3ed8ff636566e1c36f8f496d9423a371045dde76" :answer/id #uuid "590c92b3-0e25-5ee5-98b1-112d0c45cdba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,x=-\\frac{1}{3},\\,x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39793/selection/4c03f190894711395bf29a179b7ee393635b4992702e4e376354f7894b674161" :answer/id #uuid "7f6505de-f1a8-52d6-a334-7bdc05c3815f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3,\\,x=1,\\,x=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39793/selection/4d02ef9c758cbeec5a5ddb2fc04dfda2a159aec04eaaaff1ac89d30507dc8efc" :answer/id #uuid "d8612c72-3c4f-5932-957f-68ddfb91d377" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-3,\\,x=-1,\\,x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39793/selection/d94d1e53a20d0dae228254bfcf192be11dcfa06ef75c4404232d7c27bc2aec57" :answer/id #uuid "486c9506-60ba-525a-a798-d496693df2c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39793/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed6b8764-edab-5b6d-94cd-954f90ed2b1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39793/selection/4d02ef9c758cbeec5a5ddb2fc04dfda2a159aec04eaaaff1ac89d30507dc8efc" :answer-field/choices ["q-39793/selection/390fd85541da345662d60af73357478ba9af6adedb24874b4dcb74a371c5519f" "q-39793/selection/dab6bca13f296cb6500ebc2a3ed8ff636566e1c36f8f496d9423a371045dde76" "q-39793/selection/4c03f190894711395bf29a179b7ee393635b4992702e4e376354f7894b674161" "q-39793/selection/4d02ef9c758cbeec5a5ddb2fc04dfda2a159aec04eaaaff1ac89d30507dc8efc" "q-39793/selection/d94d1e53a20d0dae228254bfcf192be11dcfa06ef75c4404232d7c27bc2aec57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39793" :question/id #uuid "ca4d349e-c1ee-5a19-a1e0-b0c9e7e02dd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-39793" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{x}{(x+3)(x+1)(x-1)}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)(x+1)(x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the three solutions $x=-3,$ $x=-1$ and $x=1.$ Therefore, the equations of the vertical asymptotes are  $x=-3,\\,$ $x=-1$ and $x=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39793/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60c99086-75e7-5d91-b425-4e1b6f582bcc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39793"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278534/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "826f3f8f-fce5-5a53-8788-7a664039f20c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278534/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f0153af-058d-5fa1-8a99-a0ad23bc889e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278534/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-278534/field-1/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278534/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6cb2e42c-5eb3-5dda-ac03-b18f06a9ae40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278534/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "8dadeb61-47fb-5ec9-9779-cfb08f315c90" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278534/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-278534/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278534" :question/id #uuid "7c02d208-ab50-59ab-9034-5180c0ab1f28" :question/math-academy-id "q-278534" :question/is-example false :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x+5}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nAdding both fractions and then factoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{1}{x+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+5)+(x-1)}{(x-1)(x+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x+10+x-1}{(x-1)(x+5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3x+9}{(x-1)(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)(x+5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives the two solutions $x=-5$ and $x=1.$ \n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the equations of the vertical asymptotes are $x=-5$ and $x=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-278534/field-1" "q-278534/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60c99086-75e7-5d91-b425-4e1b6f582bcc"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278534"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39931/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" :answer/id #uuid "1b595521-b5ed-5849-95a6-bb85abcb2af5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function has no vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39931/selection/8dd0139fe2bdff82a7de02af21e81b3fb0031e695d60709e4cec3b9cfa395bee" :answer/id #uuid "6ffcef3c-dfff-5cc5-865f-6a93368f8aca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39931/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "86e6a4e9-3536-597d-ad53-dd682e7a8693" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39931/selection/565f087efc172cc689d6ac7a38ae1818e245a6f8995ecba68bcdf0ac5950b2ea" :answer/id #uuid "033f2964-5658-5c3d-8d41-5f8b8f03f6b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39931/selection/d94d1e53a20d0dae228254bfcf192be11dcfa06ef75c4404232d7c27bc2aec57" :answer/id #uuid "aaf56efe-3c49-56fb-a4f6-13996b0e5994" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39931/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6068a0f2-0fc5-5933-91e4-4558939123aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39931/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer-field/choices ["q-39931/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" "q-39931/selection/8dd0139fe2bdff82a7de02af21e81b3fb0031e695d60709e4cec3b9cfa395bee" "q-39931/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" "q-39931/selection/565f087efc172cc689d6ac7a38ae1818e245a6f8995ecba68bcdf0ac5950b2ea" "q-39931/selection/d94d1e53a20d0dae228254bfcf192be11dcfa06ef75c4404232d7c27bc2aec57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39931" :question/id #uuid "7f79f42d-8b5c-5d47-bdfd-d09cbfb2f9d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-39931" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)(x+2)}{{x}^{2}(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-2)\\cancel{(x+2)}}{{x}^{2}\\cancel{(x+2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=0\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $x=0.$ Therefore, $x=0$ is the only vertical asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-39931/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53b26ee4-53af-5660-a9e6-8e5cca8b3e1d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39931"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278545/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b97cc287-7d92-5b2f-86e3-a1dd8cb4b12c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278545/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "4cd1a1d2-f7c4-568b-a2a1-2c56085af28f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278545/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7481fd3-ff5f-51be-999e-837b4dcbeefe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278545/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-278545/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-278545/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278545/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "e336a1f1-a8a2-5693-a6b1-a00bc815cd9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278545/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "17876d32-327c-5ed4-89d8-85a2e4d81fb3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278545/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-278545/field-2/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278545" :question/id #uuid "0121bdef-ddb8-5058-ac4a-7e4de52c39cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-278545" :question/is-example false :question/problem "In **ascending order**, the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4x+4}$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}-4x+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}(x-1)-4(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+2}{({x}^{2}-4)(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+2}{(x-2)(x+2)(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x+2}}{(x-2)\\cancel{(x+2)}(x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(x-2)(x-1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n(x-2)(x-1)=0\n$$\n\nThis gives the solutions $x=1$ and $x=2.$ \n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the equations of the vertical asymptotes are $x=1$ and $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278545/field-1" "q-278545/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53b26ee4-53af-5660-a9e6-8e5cca8b3e1d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278545"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39804/selection/3d9482eabd5d50942c08e64fff899b513485e524b397ba3c1855281c08d34888" :answer/id #uuid "2c143f3f-f895-5523-bd8e-a8c5ba762b97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-5$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39804/selection/155dd265639e878b8a1c91ae83acdec6ace634fdf5ab106c3054d6bbcf26c71b" :answer/id #uuid "f5ae5a22-7a44-5333-9d77-fb5d218f2c23" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39804/selection/832f1a5fa3462eea89cbfdbf8e899120f1fd993be70aaaf11fef0a80136be2fd" :answer/id #uuid "b538ced9-1921-5056-8a6c-f23516d3216c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-5,\\,x=-1,\\,x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39804/selection/565f087efc172cc689d6ac7a38ae1818e245a6f8995ecba68bcdf0ac5950b2ea" :answer/id #uuid "5c1eacb0-27c9-5c05-9972-65b812b5f62b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=1$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3