ical asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-39804/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53b26ee4-53af-5660-a9e6-8e5cca8b3e1d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39804"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-278556/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "584490c8-bb45-5595-b731-1d7d57c888b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278556/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "dbff07c6-1dbf-55a6-bc8e-0d01a7132d8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-278556/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "21854994-875f-54e3-bd78-266d4e50f132" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-278556/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-278556/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-278556/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-278556" :question/id #uuid "ed5b9586-6f8d-5e4e-bcf4-a37872276132" :question/math-academy-id "q-278556" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{2x-1}{2{x}^{2}+x-1}$ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2x-1}{2{x}^{2}+x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-1}{(x+1)(2x-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2x-1}}{(x+1)\\cancel{(2x-1)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\nx+1=0\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $x=-1.$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the vertical asymptote is $x=-1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-278556/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53b26ee4-53af-5660-a9e6-8e5cca8b3e1d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-278556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80691/selection/54249fde4686e1c70a6f781fae137408f8ae3c0b8523c64caab897117e819d81" :answer/id #uuid "07ffc3fb-8526-58f8-8e45-ee45883509f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,\\,x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80691/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "1c72a0f1-a3ad-5fa3-b450-f3b1983bf276" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80691/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" :answer/id #uuid "dbde9959-92de-5a71-9916-adb91be4172e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80691/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer/id #uuid "73ef5ac6-2d11-5c0f-9771-005cd171f65b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80691/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" :answer/id #uuid "9bccf02f-24d5-5650-ac8f-66cba72237f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function has no vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80691/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0446ce53-7377-5e26-b7d5-3668e465def9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80691/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer-field/choices ["q-80691/selection/54249fde4686e1c70a6f781fae137408f8ae3c0b8523c64caab897117e819d81" "q-80691/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" "q-80691/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" "q-80691/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" "q-80691/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80691" :question/id #uuid "4e962760-f3da-5333-9a7a-01dcad931ed8" :question/math-academy-id "q-80691" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Calculate the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+2}{x(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{x+2}}{x\\cancel{(x+2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\nx=0\n$$\n\nThis gives the solution $x=0.$ Therefore, $x=0$ is the only vertical asymptote." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80691/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "53b26ee4-53af-5660-a9e6-8e5cca8b3e1d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39795"] :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{5}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\nx({x}^{2}+x+1)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $2x=0$ gives the solution $x=0.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+x+1=0$ has no real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & ={1}^{2}-4(1)(1) \\\\  & =1-4 \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-270003/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "f17f0b1f-6926-5b07-afaf-eb5245098b37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270003/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "ec861ded-03c9-5f56-bfe6-21787fd8f3b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-270003/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "151a1256-0239-5a7c-9590-a11ed93d9436" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-270003/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-270003/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-270003/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-270003" :question/id #uuid "9ae77e5d-b0f9-5b02-9b75-f438323421b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-270003" :question/is-example false :question/problem "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{2x-3}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+5x-20}$ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2x-3}{{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+5x-20} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-3}{{x}^{2}(x-4)+5(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-3}{({x}^{2}+5)(x-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+5)(x-4)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $x-4=0$ gives the solution $x=4.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+5=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptote is $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-270003/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b18ace11-d31c-5d5a-bd2e-32e1c28af2b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-270003"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80676/selection/caa1480127d61a1777b06d605f1adffc9022d9830425fbcfd75797676392e878" :answer/id #uuid "559a96b6-a96c-5b10-9ddf-38fcbe5f9065" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80676/selection/e2fb81eb51aa22590b0d7d031cbd4d3810faa2649578c41d091ea7391a3293a2" :answer/id #uuid "ee6d8f23-7ff8-5cd6-99e8-5b8c8de6e3df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,\\,x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80676/selection/09ac6fe94454773d85dceeb177336c7b49f6b58b9256122a1ba8c93dd15f29cd" :answer/id #uuid "bfd4a485-af18-53f2-89de-db046518bd02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,\\,x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80676/selection/f2d0f5c0341066fddb62cf1064d5cdf4169d5bb9201989c85ce2b2a732fb48b4" :answer/id #uuid "3eda7e06-233e-5ff0-a938-24550d939573" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,\\,x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80676/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer/id #uuid "c1a88c2c-d0b4-5719-a479-95cee5741f53" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80676/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0d747a6-c6d2-5c6a-8e21-9b79e1af9248" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-80676/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer-field/choices ["q-80676/selection/caa1480127d61a1777b06d605f1adffc9022d9830425fbcfd75797676392e878" "q-80676/selection/e2fb81eb51aa22590b0d7d031cbd4d3810faa2649578c41d091ea7391a3293a2" "q-80676/selection/09ac6fe94454773d85dceeb177336c7b49f6b58b9256122a1ba8c93dd15f29cd" "q-80676/selection/f2d0f5c0341066fddb62cf1064d5cdf4169d5bb9201989c85ce2b2a732fb48b4" "q-80676/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-80676" :question/id #uuid "3a048473-3fcb-5d1a-a119-0fd9e80272ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-80676" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Calculate the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+4x-8}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+4x-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-1}{{x}^{2}(x-2)+4(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x-1}{({x}^{2}+4)(x-2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+4)(x-2)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $x-2=0$ gives the solution $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+4=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-80676/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b18ace11-d31c-5d5a-bd2e-32e1c28af2b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80676"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113527/selection/b3f3cd259eab6f19c0c66e87049fb8d420b48392fd29c0b9bdd7146165731a8c" :answer/id #uuid "d964613e-fcda-5f09-8c63-a405fd222a5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=6$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113527/selection/0b71ed31b54db2f2e7ec707b0a04499a5069d7189b0811622a9ab373f5143838" :answer/id #uuid "d1c605ad-69c9-580d-8218-af950816c14b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=6$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113527/selection/a7ed344b50d5edb489432f4c6385c162d248906a53bcad9b06e8da7e3df875f8" :answer/id #uuid "0ed3e03b-2b97-5daa-af26-00ec3fa514f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-6$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113527/selection/017ec74e48021b90d41305ba8cdc32b5df2a5e0d6620fb190ddde80f6dd00a99" :answer/id #uuid "e07bcdb7-1b3b-5227-8965-90e8e187ede5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113527/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer/id #uuid "2112feaf-e9d9-5a3d-ae9a-465d4aa43900" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113527/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aff3477f-6944-59c3-b10c-0345d482afc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113527/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer-field/choices ["q-113527/selection/b3f3cd259eab6f19c0c66e87049fb8d420b48392fd29c0b9bdd7146165731a8c" "q-113527/selection/0b71ed31b54db2f2e7ec707b0a04499a5069d7189b0811622a9ab373f5143838" "q-113527/selection/a7ed344b50d5edb489432f4c6385c162d248906a53bcad9b06e8da7e3df875f8" "q-113527/selection/017ec74e48021b90d41305ba8cdc32b5df2a5e0d6620fb190ddde80f6dd00a99" "q-113527/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113527" :question/id #uuid "046b8096-a4b3-5639-81fd-05cfaf3fcc14" :question/math-academy-id "q-113527" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-12}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x:$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+6x-12} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{{x}^{2}(x-2)+6(x-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+3)(x-3)}{({x}^{2}+6)(x-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+6)(x-2)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $x-2=0$ gives the solution $x=2.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+6=0$ has no real solutions.\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-113527/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b18ace11-d31c-5d5a-bd2e-32e1c28af2b9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113527"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-80679"] :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-4x+5=0.\n$$\n\nNote that the above equation has no real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =(-4{)}^{2}-4(1)(5) \\\\  & =16-20 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-39936/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" :answer/id #uuid "2350bf6f-029a-56e7-8eed-ce2d4597c2b0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function has no vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39936/selection/5b073700a15034eef9d86418d2beb7a48945becaf327bea65b414b48e0abd8e1" :answer/id #uuid "39edf0a9-3626-50b6-b8ac-c6377332b536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39936/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "0d883f3b-2ee6-533d-8554-e299230631e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39936/selection/5139cf2d6dba3e22693f56615514fd256362a4974df5eec86b4ba2978b3085fc" :answer/id #uuid "01a4901a-d086-5832-946f-ab7856a1fa96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-1,\\,x=0,\\,x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39936/selection/4db00e9322f062eaebe516a8deeab76cec77fe41c310e73c913ce3613d869b43" :answer/id #uuid "0e192115-e897-5b7b-b1a5-fca98400565e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{1}{2},\\,x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39936/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "18f59d0c-7f4f-5f14-a8bf-a98307102924" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39936/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" :answer-field/choices ["q-39936/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" "q-39936/selection/5b073700a15034eef9d86418d2beb7a48945becaf327bea65b414b48e0abd8e1" "q-39936/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" "q-39936/selection/5139cf2d6dba3e22693f56615514fd256362a4974df5eec86b4ba2978b3085fc" "q-39936/selection/4db00e9322f062eaebe516a8deeab76cec77fe41c310e73c913ce3613d869b43"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39936" :question/id #uuid "10e486fb-a153-567a-b122-83eab72817c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-39936" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{4}-1}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{{x}^{4}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-1}{({x}^{2}-1)({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-1)(x+1)}{(x-1)(x+1)({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x-1)(x+1)}}{\\cancel{(x-1)(x+1)}({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+1=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-39936/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39936"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-80696/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "ebbbcb59-c692-531d-9274-f1ef43b872e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80696/selection/afd3eb9e977d1120fb3c3b6a691427283ab0f92faffdd99fff2cc64fe37472f9" :answer/id #uuid "8059f82e-e48a-532f-adf4-5db8e1c8ba05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0,\\,x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-80696/selection