 get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{4x}{x({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cancel{x}}{\\cancel{x}({x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{{x}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+1=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-80696/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-80696"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113554/selection/19d31c643e0669c1235c77d22af8aa11eb3c0cd7944087d6bb91550bc4735345" :answer/id #uuid "9483f33d-2de1-5f76-8fe8-e0fca53b7172" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113554/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" :answer/id #uuid "7f554535-ede4-51cf-9470-9f28aab72341" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The function has no vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113554/selection/6385bb403aacee362671876f7e4dc8c4419cebbf9f1608b5c76f83e5ba7a3232" :answer/id #uuid "7b29c80e-0081-5110-bde7-2ab508f0b0a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=\\sqrt{3}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113554/selection/4c3e66f1638ae14e3052cfa1f8b6660792742045dae43776f36de41dd9ee9e00" :answer/id #uuid "f4640ffd-657d-529c-8dbc-10f5e811b562" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-\\sqrt{3},x=0$ and $x=\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113554/selection/e2f70a7d8884fe126e594093708dce0f237fb9146d3407e43441c37ae1ac59d2" :answer/id #uuid "9d936e93-b5b8-59f1-91e9-c12a6e94cc65" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=-3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-113554/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0cc2b385-a50a-5c79-bfee-a5205565d2d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-113554/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" :answer-field/choices ["q-113554/selection/19d31c643e0669c1235c77d22af8aa11eb3c0cd7944087d6bb91550bc4735345" "q-113554/selection/e5d103e2c07ae759d9eddce65c552ccfa6a5a00acf0aea2f18942b9a819f2577" "q-113554/selection/6385bb403aacee362671876f7e4dc8c4419cebbf9f1608b5c76f83e5ba7a3232" "q-113554/selection/4c3e66f1638ae14e3052cfa1f8b6660792742045dae43776f36de41dd9ee9e00" "q-113554/selection/e2f70a7d8884fe126e594093708dce0f237fb9146d3407e43441c37ae1ac59d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-113554" :question/id #uuid "e0085fda-c140-5022-a903-4aa2d0060987" :question/math-academy-id "q-113554" :question/is-example false :question/problem "Determine the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{2{x}^{2}-6}{{x}^{4}-9}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}-6}{{x}^{4}-9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2({x}^{2}-3)}{({x}^{2}-3)({x}^{2}+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cancel{({x}^{2}-3)}}{\\cancel{({x}^{2}-3)}({x}^{2}+3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+3=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions. Therefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-113554/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-113554"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-113545/selection/565f087efc172cc689d6ac7a38ae1818e245a6f8995ecba68bcdf0ac5950b2ea" :answer/id #uuid "de0199e2-7a70